From a7ae9fadb0896ef4df7c578b82c72f71a0e3e475 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:51:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Forge host: friend match table starts whoever wins the
 toss; players see each other

- Bridge: in a friend match the seat that is not asked to act first never got a
  prompt to publish, so it kept reporting "initializing". The gateway's /ready
  reads seat 1, so whenever the guest won the coin toss the table never became
  ready and both players timed out (startup_deadline last ready 503). Each seat
  now publishes when the game starts, and publishes board changes as they
  arrive (nothing paces the other person's plays the way CPU steps are paced).
  Reproduced and verified on the real host bridge: seeds where seat 2 goes
  first now report running on both seats, and both players can keep and play.
- Rooms: create and join take an optional player card {name, image, crop};
  the room view returns the other player's card as `opponent`. Only a
  sanitised name (40 chars), an https image and a bounded crop are kept.
- Tests: friend-match player-card test. Pins re-bound; verify-inputs,
  run-static-checks, npm check, NativeHumanPriorityProof,
  NativePaymentTransitionChecks and NativeStartingPlayerChecks pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G4m5sRQtg4L7gdECz4hmKi
