From 8a2742b3c7cb812a2c086f3f5492518e383f1268 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:32:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Forge host: friend challenges (one friend, five minutes,
 quiet "not now")

- POST /api/play/rooms takes an optional `to` (a friend's account id): the room
  becomes a challenge only that account can see or join, open for five minutes.
- GET /api/play/rooms lists the challenges waiting for the caller, each with
  the invite that opens it, the format, the sender's id and their player card.
- DELETE /api/play/rooms/<id> by the challenged friend ends it as "declined"
  (the host's room view says so); the host's own DELETE still cancels.
- A challenge's invite opens only for the named friend; the room view marks
  `challenge: true`. Expired challenge lists are swept with the room cleanup.
- Tests: two friend-match tests (who sees it, decline, expiry, self-challenge
  refused, accept starts the match). Pins re-bound; verify-inputs,
  run-static-checks and npm check (237) pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G4m5sRQtg4L7gdECz4hmKi
